# Barreletics Design System — section library (HARD)

We are building a **reusable Shopify section library**, not a homepage. Homepage is only the first template that assembles **approved** sections later.

## Workflow (non-negotiable)

1. Build **ONE** section
2. QA that section
3. Review/refine until Andrew approves
4. **Freeze** its architecture
5. Only then begin the next section

- **Reference implementation:** `shopify-build/sections/home-split-hero.liquid` (+ `assets/heroes.css`)
- **Frozen only after explicit Andrew architecture + code approval**
- **Blocked until freeze:** `hero-fullbleed`, `collection-split-hero`, and every other new marketing section
- Do **not** assemble a homepage deliverable ahead of approved sections
- Optimize for world-class reusable design system, **not** speed

## Architecture (every major component)

| Requirement | Rule |
|-------------|------|
| File | Own `sections/*.liquid` |
| Schema | Complete Shopify schema + `presets` (Theme Editor addable) |
| Editor | Independently draggable / removable / reusable |
| Shared code | `snippets/` + shared assets only |
| Coupling | No section depends on another section |
| Scope | No page-specific or monolithic architecture |

## Anti-patterns (reject)

- Building multiple new sections in one pass
- Homepage-only Liquid/CSS that cannot live on another template
- Hard dependencies on sibling sections or fixed page order
- Monolithic “page” sections that own multiple compositions
- Starting next section before the current one is frozen

